# harness/field/field.env.example: the field run's inputs that are not in git. Copy it to
# ~/kerber-lab/field.env (mode 0600; run.sh refuses a file others can read) and fill it in. run.sh sources it
# when it exists; a scenario that needs a value it lacks fails, it is never skipped.

# The satomlin kit copy a scenario installs from, and the sha256 of its tarball. nfs-client and sssd-login do
# not read them: their baseline snapshots are already joined and carry the kit's lab copies (nfs-client checks
# their sha256), and services feeds the kit's check_spnego from lib/check_spnego.lab.sh.
FIELD_KIT_DIR=$HOME/kerber-lab/kit/satomlin-kit
FIELD_KIT_SHA256=

# KLLDAP (klldap-swap): the checkout scratch copies come from (git archive of the pin, never a copy of the
# working tree) and the pinned commit; the phase-80 fixture (an MIT db2 KDC directory krb5kdc/ and an LLDAP
# data/ directory, only read); Zepmann/lldap-cli for phase 85 (only read: the run uses a copy).
FIELD_KLLDAP_REPO=$HOME/Projects/klldap
FIELD_KLLDAP_PIN=079a56484504eade368eaaa398c580a496b72d8f
FIELD_KLLDAP_FIXTURE=$HOME/Projects/test-klldap
FIELD_LLDAP_CLI=$HOME/kerber-lab/klldap/lldap-cli/lldap-cli

# The AD lab's environment file (0600). redact.py and scan-secrets.py read every value in it (default
# ~/adlab/env); ad-trust reads the AD accounts from it.
FIELD_ADLAB_ENV=$HOME/adlab/env

# Optional: a Python that imports winrm (pywinrm) for ad-trust's DC scripts (default: python3).
# FIELD_WINRM_PY=$HOME/kerber-lab/venv/winrm/bin/python

# Optional: the repository run.sh archives the ref under test from (default: the one run.sh lives in).
# FIELD_REPO=$HOME/Projects/kerber-rust

# Optional: a prebuilt diffsend for pkinit's PK.b17 (cargo build -p krb5-tools --bin diffsend --features
# krb5-kdc/test-hooks, built in the rust-dev distrobox so it is a Fedora binary the lab VMs run). The cell pipes
# it to the leg's KDC to send the seven faulted PKINIT signatures OpenSSL 3.5 logs as "provider signature
# failure", MIT first; unset, PK.b17 is skipped (that error code, 80, is MIT = ours in the CI differential).
# FIELD_DIFFSEND=$HOME/Projects/kerber-rust/target/debug/diffsend

# Optional: the time limits, in seconds: a scenario's (default 1800) and each command's (default 900, cut to
# what is left of the scenario's).
# FIELD_SCENARIO_TIMEOUT=1800
# FIELD_CMD_TIMEOUT=900
